About CAIS &nbsp; &nbsp; 
 CAIS is the pioneer in democratizing access to and education about alternative investments for independent financial advisors, empowering them to engage and transact with leading asset managers on a massive scale through a wide variety of alternative investment products and technology solutions. CAIS provides financial advisors with a broad selection of alternative investment strategies, including hedge funds, private equity, private credit, real estate, digital assets, and structured notes. CAIS also delivers industry-leading technology, operational efficiency, and world-class client service throughout the pre-trade, trade, and post-trade experience. CAIS serves over 2,500 wealth management firms that support more than 65,000 financial advisors who oversee approximately $8.5 trillion in end-client assets. &nbsp; 
 About the Role &nbsp; 
 CAIS is hiring an Applied AI Engineer to put AI to work inside our business teams in NYC. You will be embedded with non-engineering functions such as Sales, Finance, Operations, and Client Service. You will learn how their work actually gets done, build AI-enabled workflows that save them real time, and make sure those workflows get adopted. You are an engineer first and write code regularly, but you are equally comfortable sitting with a team, mapping a process, and teaching people to use what you built. &nbsp; 
 Key Responsibilities &nbsp; 
 Embed with business teams to understand their workflows and find the highest-value opportunities for AI and automation, prioritizing by impact, feasibility, and risk &nbsp; 
 Build working solutions yourself: LLM-powered tools, agents, automations, and integrations with our enterprise systems and data sources, using approved tooling &nbsp; 
 Take prototypes to production-ready by working with engineering, data, and platform teams on deployment, testing, and maintenance &nbsp; 
 Work with Security, Compliance, and Legal so everything you build meets our governance, privacy, and confidentiality requirements &nbsp; 
 Run hands-on training and change adoption within each team, and track whether people are still using what you built months later. &nbsp; 
 Define success measures up front (time saved, error reduction, adoption) and report on results honestly, including what didn’t work &nbsp; 
 Turn what you learn into reusable patterns, templates, and playbooks so the next team starts further ahead &nbsp; 
 Skills &amp; Experience&nbsp; &nbsp; 
 Required &nbsp; 
 Strong software engineering ability, with practical experience in Python/Kotlin/TypeScript or a comparable language and in working with APIs &nbsp; 
 4+ years in Software Engineering, forward-deployed engineering, or applied AI &nbsp; 
 Hands-on experience building with LLMs, such as prompt design, tool use or agents, retrieval, and evaluating output quality and failure modes. You’ve shipped LLM-powered tools or agents that real users depend on. &nbsp; 
 Experience delivering technology or automation projects with business stakeholders in a regulated or otherwise complex enterprise environment &nbsp; 
 Clear communication with executives, business users, and engineers alike &nbsp; 
 Sound judgment about data sensitivity, security, and where automation shouldn’t be used &nbsp; 
 Preferred &nbsp; 
 Background in financial services, wealth management, or fintech &nbsp; 
 Experience with Salesforce, Snowflake, and workflow automation platforms &nbsp; 
 Experience in training, enablement
